content.text:
Use the **local branch version**, not the installed npm package.

### 1. Add a temporary test helper

This gives you predictable extension-status and waiting-for-user checks:

```bash
cat > /tmp/pi-statusline-smoke.ts <<'EOF'
import type { ExtensionAPI } from "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent";

export default function (pi: ExtensionAPI) {
  pi.registerCommand("smoke", {
    description: "Exercise footer statuses and user prompts",
    handler: async (_args, ctx) => {
      ctx.ui.setStatus("smoke-a", "🧪 项目 é — smoke test");
      ctx.ui.setStatus("smoke-b", "Second extension status");
      await ctx.ui.confirm("Smoke test", "Check the footer, then choose either answer.");
    },
  });

  pi.registerCommand("smoke-clear", {
    description: "Remove test statuses",
    handler: async (_args, ctx) => {
      ctx.ui.setStatus("smoke-a", undefined);
      ctx.ui.setStatus("smoke-b", undefined);
    },
  });
}
EOF
```

### 2. Start an isolated fullscreen session

```bash
cd /Users/feniix/src/personal/pi/pi-extensions

pi --no-extensions --no-session \
  -e ./packages/pi-statusline/extensions/index.ts \
  -e /tmp/pi-statusline-smoke.ts \
  --tui-mode fullscreen \
  --use-theme dark
```

`--no-extensions` disables installed/discovered extensions while retaining explicit `-e` files, avoiding duplicate statusline loading. `--no-session` avoids saving this test conversation.

### 3. Check these behaviors

| Action | Expected |
|---|---|
| Inspect startup | Exactly two footer lines; sensible model/context/git labels |
| Resize to roughly 40, 80, then 120 columns | No wrapping, broken emoji, overflow, or stale fragments |
| Run `/smoke` | Unicode status text appears; activity says **waiting for user** |
| Dismiss the confirmation | Activity returns to its previous state |
| Run `/smoke-clear` | Both status messages disappear |
| Change effort through `/thinking` | Footer updates immediately |
| Ask: “Run `sleep 3` using bash, then explain what you did.” | Activity transitions through responding/tool work, then returns to **idle** |
| Inspect token totals afterward | Totals do not disappear or visibly double when streaming finishes |

At narrow widths, **context should lead line one**, and **activity/statuses should lead line two**.

The model prompt uses your normal credentials and may incur usage charges.

### 4. Repeat with regular mode and a light theme

Exit pi, then run the same command with:

```bash
--tui-mode regular --use-theme light
```

Repeat resizing, `/smoke`, and `/smoke-clear`. Look especially for readable colors and footer artifacts in terminal scrollback.

**Optional:** use `/compact` after some conversation and `/tree` to navigate history. Context/totals should refresh without another prompt.

### 5. Report results

Comment on [PR #148](https://github.com/feniix/pi-extensions/pull/148) with terminal name, pi version, modes tested, and any screenshots of glitches. Remove the helper afterward:

```bash
rm /tmp/pi-statusline-smoke.ts
```

